  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1211 AM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nA few showers and storms may linger into Friday across West\nCentral Texas, but the weekend looks drier as the upper level\nridge builds back across the area. Temperatures climb back into\nthe upper 90s or just above the 100 degree mark. \n\nPattern does change for next week as the ridge weakens and then\nrecenters over the Southeast US. This provides a better fetch of \nmoisture at all levels off the Gulf and afternoon dewpoints will \nlikely remain in the 60s each afternoon rather than dropping off. \nIts a pattern where hitting the 100 degree mark usually becomes \nmore difficult, although maybe not this year with such dry \nconditions ongoing and soil moisture and evapotranspiration at a \nminimum. Currently a dry forecast for next week although would not\nbe a surprise with the better Gulf moisture fetch to see an \nenhanced sea breeze work some afternoon convection into the \nsoutheast counties on some of those days.",
